  "instructions": [
    "Heat the tandoor to 425\u000300F (220\u000300C).",
    "Brush the chicken thighs with olive oil and season with salt, black pepper, and rosemary.",
    "Place the chicken thighs in the tandoor and cook for 15 minutes.",
    "Remove the chicken from the tandoor and set aside.",
    "In the same tandoor, cook the chopped onion and ginger over medium heat for 5 minutes.",
    "Add the dried cherries, cumin, cinnamon, paprika, turmeric, salt, and black pepper to the tandoor.",
    "Stir to combine and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add the chicken broth to the tandoor and bring to a boil.",
    "Return the chicken thighs to the tandoor and cook for an additional 15 minutes.",
    "Remove the chicken from the tandoor and let rest for 5 minutes before serving.",
    "Serve the chicken thighs in the traditional clay bento-box with the flavorful sauce spooned over the top."
